        <p class="profile-detail-region">Culture · Egypt &amp; North Africa</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Garamantes</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a> region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, centred on the Wadi al-Ajjal; their capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garama">Garama</a> lay at modern Germa, about 150 km west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabha-libya">Sabha</a>, with an earlier capital at Zinkekara; other sites include Fewet, Saniat bin Huwaydi, and the southern oases of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghat">Ghat</a> and Barkat</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">Settlement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a> at least as early as 1000 BC; a powerful polity from the 6th century BC; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/foggara">foggara</a> irrigation appearing between 200 BC and 200 CE; a major regional power from the mid-2nd century AD; the end of the kingdom in the late 7th century AD</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/foggara">foggara</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qanat">qanat</a>) irrigation tapping fossil water; the first urban society in a major desert not centred on a river; control of trade routes between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-bend">Niger Bend</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slave-raiding">slave raiding</a> and trading; inscriptions in a Libyan script that are only partly decipherable; conflict with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">Greco-Roman writers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> in the 5th century BC to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliny-the-elder">Pliny the Elder</a>, Ptolemy and Solinus; excavations at Germa in the 1960s; satellite imagery published in 2011; skeletal and isotopic studies by Sergi (1951), Chamla (1968), Mattingly et al. (2003), Lahr et al. (2010), Nikita et al. (2011), Ricci et al. (2013) and Power et al. (2019)</span></div>
